    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1950-p11.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Rewrite the formula as \\[ C=\\frac{e}{\\frac{R}{n}+r}. \\] As positive \\(n\\) increases, \\(\\frac{R}{n}\\) decreases, so the positive denominator decreases while the numerator remains fixed. Therefore \\(C\\) increases.\n\nThus, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Divide the numerator and denominator by \\(n\\)",
        "As positive \\(n\\) grows, \\(\\frac{R}{n}\\) decreases"
      ],
